content.text:
That's fine, not load-bearing. I have everything needed. Let me write the plan.

## Implementation Plan: 4 additions to the "tiket" venue feature

Ground truth in the prompt is accurate on every point I checked (RPC signature, table shapes, `ticket-actions.ts`, `ticket-pos-screen.tsx` state, `pos/page.tsx` fetch, members CRUD reusability, ticket-reports pages, CSV export pattern, cashier-session doc comment, customer picker in `pos-screen.tsx`, `addTicketCategory`'s `23505` handling). No corrections needed there. I flag a few design decisions below where I'd choose a specific approach, and one item I think is wrong in the ground truth's assumption (uniqueness scope for `manual_number`).

---

### 1. Migration — `supabase/migrations/20260706300000_ticket_manual_number.sql`

**Flag before finalizing:** I'd scope the `manual_number` uniqueness the same as your guess — `(business_id, ticket_category_id, manual_number)` — but I'd make it a **partial unique index**, not a table constraint, filtering nothing extra (no rows to exclude — every serial has a manual number after backfill), just to keep it consistent stylistically with the existing partial unique indexes in this migration set (`ticket_categories_business_id_name_key`, `members_business_id_member_code_key` both use `where deleted_at is null`-style partial indexes). Since `ticket_serials` has no `deleted_at`, a plain `unique index` (not `where` filtered) is correct and simplest — no disagreement with your scope choice itself, just implementation as an index vs. inline constraint (functionally identical, either is fine; I use an index below for consistency with the file's own indexing style).

One thing to double check with you: should `manual_number` uniqueness be scoped per category, or could the same physical booklet be shared/reused across categories (e.g. Pengunjung and Penunggu draw numbers from the same physical roll)? If the venue uses **one shared paper booklet across all categories**, scoping to `(business_id, ticket_category_id, manual_number)` would wrongly allow the same physical number on both a Pengunjung and a Penunggu ticket. If each category has its own separate booklet (which matches how `serial_no` already works — separate `next_serial` counter per category), your scope is correct. I'll proceed with `(business_id, ticket_category_id, manual_number)` per your instruction, but flagged this so you can override to `(business_id, manual_number)` if it's actually one shared booklet.

Full SQL:

```sql
-- Module: manual physical ticket number per unit, in addition to the
-- existing auto serial_no. Paper booklets are numbered by hand; the
-- physical number typed by the cashier must be recorded per ticket for
-- reconciliation against physical stock, alongside (not replacing) the
-- existing continuous serial_no sequence.

-- Backfill-safe: 4 existing test rows get manual_number = serial_no as text
-- so the column can be made NOT NULL in the same migration.
alter table public.ticket_serials
  add column manual_number text;

update public.ticket_serials
  set manual_number = serial_no::text
  where manual_number is null;

alter table public.ticket_serials
  alter column manual_number set not null;

alter table public.ticket_serials
  add constraint ticket_serials_manual_number_not_blank
  check (length(trim(manual_number)) > 0);

-- Scoped like serial_no: one physical booklet assumed per category.
-- If a venue instead shares one physical booklet across categories,
-- this should be (business_id, manual_number) instead — confirm before
-- relying on this constraint.
create unique index ticket_serials_business_id_category_id_manual_number_key
  on public.ticket_serials (business_id, ticket_category_id, manual_number);

-- checkout_ticket_transaction: p_items shape changes from
-- [{ticket_category_id, qty}] to [{ticket_category_id, manual_numbers: string[]}].
-- Same SQL signature (jsonb param), so no drop/grant of a new overload needed —
-- create or replace in place. Pricing/holiday/member/tax/service logic is
-- byte-for-byte unchanged; only the per-unit insert loop changes shape.
create or replace function public.checkout_ticket_transaction(
  p_business_id uuid,
  p_cashier_id uuid,
  p_items jsonb, -- array of {ticket_category_id, manual_numbers: string[]}
  p_payment_method text,
  p_received numeric default null,
  p_member_id uuid default null
)
returns table (transaction_id uuid, invoice_number text)
language plpgsql
security definer
set search_path = ''
as $$
declare
  v_business record;
  v_member record;
  v_invoice_number text;
  v_seq int;
  v_is_holiday boolean;
  v_subtotal numeric(12, 2) := 0;
  v_service numeric(12, 2) := 0;
  v_tax numeric(12, 2) := 0;
  v_total numeric(12, 2);
  v_change numeric(12, 2);
  v_transaction_id uuid;
  v_shift_id uuid;
  v_item jsonb;
  v_category_id uuid;
  v_category record;
  v_manual_numbers jsonb;
  v_manual_number text;
  v_use_member_price boolean := false;
  v_unit_price numeric(12, 2);
  v_serial int;
begin
  if not private.owns_business(p_business_id) then
    raise exception 'not authorized';
  end if;

  if not exists (
    select 1 from public.cashiers c
    where c.id = p_cashier_id and c.business_id = p_business_id and c.active
  ) then
    raise exception 'invalid cashier';
  end if;

  if p_payment_method is null or length(trim(p_payment_method)) = 0 then
    raise exception 'payment method required';
  end if;

  if p_items is null or jsonb_array_length(p_items) = 0 then
    raise exception 'cart is empty';
  end if;

  select b.tax_enabled, b.tax_rate, b.service_enabled, b.service_rate
  into v_business
  from public.businesses b
  where b.id = p_business_id;

  select id into v_shift_id
  from public.shifts
  where business_id = p_business_id and closed_at is null
  limit 1;

  if v_shift_id is null then
    raise exception 'no active shift — open a shift before selling';
  end if;

  if p_member_id is not null then
    select m.id, m.valid_from, m.valid_until
    into v_member
    from public.members m
    where m.id = p_member_id
      and m.business_id = p_business_id
      and m.deleted_at is null;

    if not found then
      raise exception 'member not found';
    end if;

    if current_date < v_member.valid_from or current_date > v_member.valid_until then
      raise exception 'membership tidak aktif (kadaluarsa atau belum berlaku)';
    end if;

    v_use_member_price := true;
  end if;

  v_is_holiday := extract(dow from current_date) in (0, 6)
    or exists (
      select 1 from public.ticket_holidays h
      where h.business_id = p_business_id and h.holiday_date = current_date
    );

  select count(*) + 1 into v_seq
  from public.ticket_transactions t
  where t.business_id = p_business_id
    and t.date::date = current_date;

  v_invoice_number := 'TIX-' || to_char(current_date, 'YYYYMMDD') || '-' || lpad(v_seq::text, 4, '0');

  insert into public.ticket_transactions (
    business_id, shift_id, cashier_id, member_id, invoice_number, date,
    is_holiday, subtotal, service, tax, total, payment_method, received, change
  ) values (
    p_business_id, v_shift_id, p_cashier_id, p_member_id, v_invoice_number, now(),
    v_is_holiday, 0, 0, 0, 0, p_payment_method, p_received, 0
  )
  returning id into v_transaction_id;

  for v_item in select * from jsonb_array_elements(p_items)
  loop
    v_category_id := (v_item ->> 'ticket_category_id')::uuid;
    v_manual_numbers := v_item -> 'manual_numbers';

    if v_manual_numbers is null or jsonb_typeof(v_manual_numbers) <> 'array'
      or jsonb_array_length(v_manual_numbers) = 0 then
      raise exception 'manual ticket numbers required for category %', v_category_id;
    end if;

    select * into v_category
    from public.ticket_categories
    where id = v_category_id
      and business_id = p_business_id
      and deleted_at is null
    for update;

    if not found then
      raise exception 'ticket category not found: %', v_category_id;
    end if;

    v_unit_price := case
      when v_use_member_price then v_category.member_price
      when v_is_holiday then v_category.price_holiday
      else v_category.price_weekday
    end;

    for v_manual_number in select jsonb_array_elements_text(v_manual_numbers)
    loop
      if v_manual_number is null or length(trim(v_manual_number)) = 0 then
        raise exception 'nomor tiket fisik tidak boleh kosong (kategori %)', v_category.name;
      end if;

      v_serial := v_category.next_serial;

      insert into public.ticket_serials (
        ticket_transaction_id, ticket_category_id, business_id,
        serial_no, manual_number, price, is_member_price
      ) values (
        v_transaction_id, v_category_id, p_business_id,
        v_serial, trim(v_manual_number), v_unit_price, v_use_member_price
      );

      v_category.next_serial := v_category.next_serial + 1;
      v_subtotal := v_subtotal + v_unit_price;
    end loop;

    update public.ticket_categories
    set next_serial = v_category.next_serial
    where id = v_category_id;
  end loop;

  if v_business.service_enabled then
    v_service := round(v_subtotal * v_business.service_rate / 100);
  end if;

  if v_business.tax_enabled then
    v_tax := round((v_subtotal + v_service) * v_business.tax_rate / 100);
  end if;

  v_total := v_subtotal + v_service + v_tax;
  v_change := greatest(coalesce(p_received, v_total) - v_total, 0);

  update public.ticket_transactions
  set subtotal = v_subtotal,
      service = v_service,
      tax = v_tax,
      total = v_total,
      change = v_change
  where id = v_transaction_id;

  return query select v_transaction_id, v_invoice_number;
end;
$$;

grant execute on function public.checkout_ticket_transaction(uuid, uuid, jsonb, text, numeric, uuid) to authenticated;
```

Note: the duplicate-manual-number-within-the-same-cart-submission case (e.g. cashier types "A001" twice for the same category in one checkout) will raise a `23505` from the unique index at `insert` time inside the loop — that's fine, it aborts the whole transaction (atomic), and the client-side friendly message (step 2) handles it. No need for an explicit pre-check in PL/pgSQL; the constraint does the job and keeps the function simple.

---

### 2. `src/app/business/[businessId]/pos/ticket-actions.ts` changes

- Change `TicketCartItemInput`:
  ```ts
  export type TicketCartItemInput = {
    ticketCategoryId: string;
    manualNumbers: string[];
  };
  ```
- In `checkoutTicket`, update the empty-cart guard (`items.length === 0` stays, but also should reject if every item has an empty `manualNumbers` array — cheap client-side sanity check before hitting the RPC) and the RPC mapping:
  ```ts
  p_items: items.map((i) => ({
    ticket_category_id: i.ticketCategoryId,
    manual_numbers: i.manualNumbers,
  })),
  ```
- Update `itemCount` for `logActivity` to `items.reduce((sum, i) => sum + i.manualNumbers.length, 0)` (was `i.qty`).
- Add a `23505` catch mirroring `addTicketCategory`'s pattern. Since this is an RPC call (not a direct table insert), the error surfaces via `error.code` on the Postgres error returned by `supabase.rpc(...)` the same way — confirm `error.code === "23505"` works identically for RPC-raised constraint violations (it does; Supabase surfaces the underlying Postgres error code regardless of whether it came from a raw `insert` or one nested inside a `plpgsql` function). Friendly message: `"Nomor tiket fisik ini sudah dipakai untuk kategori ini. Cek kembali nomor booklet."`
- No changes needed to `lookupMemberByCode` or `voidTicketTransaction`.

---

### 3. `src/app/business/[businessId]/pos/ticket-pos-screen.tsx` cart UI rework

**State shape change:**
```ts
// was: const [qtyByCategory, setQtyByCategory] = useState<Record<string, number>>({});
const [unitsByCategory, setUnitsByCategory] =
  useState<Record<string, string[]>>({});
```
Each category maps to an array of manual-number strings (one string per physical ticket unit; empty string `""` = not yet typed, still counts toward qty/subtotal so the price total updates as soon as a row is added, but blocks checkout until filled).

**Replace `changeQty`** with two functional-update helpers (preserving the exact pattern that avoids stale closures — always derive next state from `prev`, never from a captured outer variable):
```ts
function addUnit(categoryId: string) {
  setUnitsByCategory((prev) => ({
    ...prev,
    [categoryId]: [...(prev[categoryId] ?? []), ""],
  }));
}

function removeUnit(categoryId: string, index: number) {
  setUnitsByCategory((prev) => {
    const next = { ...prev };
    const arr = (next[categoryId] ?? []).filter((_, i) => i !== index);
    if (arr.length === 0) {
      delete next[categoryId];
    } else {
      next[categoryId] = arr;
    }
    return next;
  });
}

function setUnitNumber(categoryId: string, index: number, value: string) {
  setUnitsByCategory((prev) => {
    const arr = [...(prev[categoryId] ?? [])];
    arr[index] = value;
    return { ...prev, [categoryId]: arr };
  });
}
```

**`cartLines` derivation** changes from `qty: qtyByCategory[c.id]` to `units: unitsByCategory[c.id] ?? []`, with `qty` derived as `units.length` wherever needed for subtotal math (`unitPrice * units.length`, unchanged formula otherwise — `unitPriceFor(category)` is untouched, still depends only on `member`/`isHoliday`, not on manual numbers).

**Category card UI** (currently a stepper `− count +`): replace with:
- A "+ Tambah tiket" button (calls `addUnit(c.id)`) that appends an empty-string row.
- Below it, if `units.length > 0`, render one row per unit: a small text input (`value={units[i]}`, `onChange` calls `setUnitNumber(c.id, i, e.target.value)`, `placeholder="No. tiket fisik"`) plus a small `✕` remove button (`removeUnit(c.id, i)`). Keep the unit count and running subtotal for that category visible (e.g. `"{units.length} tiket · Rp{price * units.length}"`) so the cashier still gets the at-a-glance count they had with the stepper.
- This is the single highest-effort UI change in the plan — with categories rendered in a `grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3`, a per-unit input list inside a narrow card gets cramped fast for higher quantities (e.g. 10 tickets = 10 stacked inputs in a ~150px-wide card). Recommend widening the category grid to full-width stacked cards (`grid-cols-1` or a flex column) instead of the current multi-column grid when in this per-unit-input mode, since text inputs need real width to be usable. Flag this to the user as a visual departure from the current stepper card layout.

**Checkout guard** in `handleConfirmPayment`: before calling `checkoutTicket`, validate every unit in every cart line has a non-blank trimmed manual number; if not, `setError("Semua nomor tiket fisik harus diisi.")` and return early (client-side pre-check mirroring the RPC's own validation, for a faster/friendlier failure than a round trip).

**`items` construction** changes to:
```ts
const items: TicketCartItemInput[] = cartLines
  .filter((l) => l.units.length > 0)
  .map((l) => ({
    ticketCategoryId: l.category.id,
    manualNumbers: l.units.map((u) => u.trim()),
  }));
```

**Cart sidebar rendering** (`cartLines.map(...)`) currently shows `"{qty}x {category.name}"` — change to `"{units.length}x {category.name}"`, unaffected otherwise. The `"Belum ada tiket dipilih"` empty-state condition (`cartLines.length === 0`) stays correct since `cartLines` is still filtered to non-empty categories.

**`resetForNextTransaction`**: change `setQtyByCategory({})` to `setUnitsByCategory({})`.

---

### 4. Member browsing + inline add, embedded in POS screen

**`src/app/business/[businessId]/pos/page.tsx`** — inside the `business.business_type === "tiket"` branch, add a members fetch mirroring the existing `customers` fetch pattern used lower in the same file for F&B/Retail:
```ts
const { data: memberRows } = await supabase
  .from("members")
  .select("id, name, phone, member_code, valid_from, valid_until")
  .eq("business_id", businessId)
  .is("deleted_at", null)
  .order("name", { ascending: true });
```
Pass `members={(memberRows ?? []).map(...)}` as a new prop to `<TicketPosScreen>`.

**New component `src/app/business/[businessId]/pos/member-panel.tsx`** (client component), replacing the current inline "Member (opsional)" box in `ticket-pos-screen.tsx`:
- Props: `businessId`, `members: Member[]` (full list, valid_from/valid_until included so client can locally flag active/expired same as the `/members` list page does), `member: Member | null`, `onSelect(member)`, `onRelease()`.
