### 5. Barcode generation for printable member card

- **Package**: add `jsbarcode` (`npm install jsbarcode`) — no disagreement with your choice; it's dependency-free, renders directly to an SVG or canvas element via a plain function call (`JsBarcode(svgElement, value, options)`), and is the de facto standard for exactly this use case in JS. No lighter alternative is meaningfully better for one component.
- **New component `src/app/business/[businessId]/(dashboard)/members/[memberId]/member-barcode.tsx`** (client component):
  ```tsx
  "use client";
  import { useEffect, useRef } from "react";
  import JsBarcode from "jsbarcode";

  export default function MemberBarcode({ value }: { value: string }) {
    const ref = useRef<SVGSVGElement>(null);
    useEffect(() => {
      if (ref.current) {
        JsBarcode(ref.current, value, { format: "CODE128", displayValue: true, height: 60 });
      }
    }, [value]);
    return <svg ref={ref} />;
  }
  ```
- **New route `src/app/business/[businessId]/(dashboard)/members/[memberId]/card/page.tsx`** (server component) mirroring `ticket-reports/[transactionId]/receipt/page.tsx`'s shape: fetch `member` by id+business scoping (`name, member_code, valid_until`), render a printable card layout (member name, code as text, `<MemberBarcode value={member.member_code} />`, `print:` Tailwind classes matching the receipt page's `print:max-w-none`/`print:hidden` conventions) plus `<PrintButton .../>`.
- **New `src/app/business/[businessId]/(dashboard)/members/[memberId]/card/print-button.tsx`** — copy of `ticket-reports/.../receipt/print-button.tsx`'s pattern exactly (back-link + `window.print()` button), just pointed at `/business/${businessId}/members/${memberId}` for the back link.
- **Wire-in**: add a link/button in `members/[memberId]/page.tsx` next to the existing header actions (near `EditMemberForm`), e.g. `<Link href={\`/business/${businessId}/members/${memberId}/card\`} target="_blank">🪪 Cetak Kartu</Link>`, styled consistent with the `"🖨️ Cetak Struk"` link already used in `ticket-reports/[transactionId]/page.tsx`.
- Barcode content = existing `member_code` text field (e.g. `M-0001`) — no schema change needed for this part; Code128 handles alphanumeric with hyphens natively.

