### 6. CSV export route — `src/app/business/[businessId]/(dashboard)/ticket-reports/export/route.ts`

Mirrors `reports/export/route.ts` exactly: same `csvEscape`/`toCsv`/BOM/`Content-Disposition` helpers (duplicate the small helper functions locally rather than sharing a module — that matches the existing codebase's choice to duplicate rather than factor out, since `reports/export/route.ts` doesn't import them from a shared lib either).

`GET` handler: `type=transactions|tickets|hourly` (default `transactions`), reusing `../../reports/period.ts`'s `parsePeriod`/`getPeriodRange` (relative path is two levels up from `ticket-reports/export/` to `reports/`, i.e. `../../reports/period`).

- **`type=transactions`** — one row per `ticket_transactions`, columns: `No. Invoice, Tanggal, Jam, Kasir, Member, Hari, Subtotal, Layanan, Pajak, Total, Metode Bayar, Diterima, Kembalian, Status`. Query `ticket_transactions` joined to `cashiers!ticket_transactions_cashier_id_fkey(name)` and `members(name, member_code)`, filtered by date range, `voided=false` optionally excluded or shown as a Status column (recommend showing voided rows with a `"Dibatalkan"` status column rather than excluding, since reconciliation needs to see voided tickets too — flag this as a deliberate difference from `reports/export/route.ts`'s `type=transactions` which does `.eq("voided", false)` and silently excludes voids; ticket reconciliation has a stronger need to see the full physical-ticket trail including voided ones).
- **`type=tickets`** — one row per `ticket_serials`, columns: `No. Invoice, Tanggal, Jam, No. Seri, No. Tiket Manual, Kategori, Harga, Member?, Status`. Query `ticket_serials` joined through `ticket_transaction_id` to the transaction header (same join shape already used in `ticket-reports/page.tsx`'s `serials`/`txMap` pattern) filtered by the date range on the transaction's `date`.
- **`type=hourly`** — aggregate revenue/count by hour-of-day (`0`-`23`) across the selected period. Since this needs to bucket by hour, it's cleanest to fetch the raw `ticket_serials` rows (with their transaction's `date`) same as `type=tickets`, then bucket in JS using `REPORT_TIMEZONE` ("Asia/Jakarta") via `new Date(iso).toLocaleString("en-US", { hour: "2-digit", hour12: false, timeZone: REPORT_TIMEZONE })` rather than a SQL `extract(hour from ...)` — SQL `extract` would use the DB session timezone (likely UTC), which would silently produce wrong hourly buckets for Jakarta time; doing the hour bucketing in JS with an explicit `timeZone` option avoids that class of bug and matches how `reports/period.ts` already handles WIB-vs-server-timezone correctness. Columns: `Jam, Jumlah Tiket, Pendapatan`. Exclude voided serials from revenue/count here (an hourly sales-volume view; showing voided tickets would misrepresent actual traffic) — this is a legitimate case for excluding voids, unlike `type=transactions`.

Filenames: `TiketTransaksi_{period}.csv`, `TiketPerUnit_{period}.csv`, `TiketPerJam_{period}.csv`.

